All 5 icons vendored. base.css ends with reduced-motion. Append selection guard after that block (or before? At very end is fine).

Note: base.css already nukes animation/transition durations under reduced motion — so CSS-module entrance animation auto-respects reduced motion globally! I can still add explicit media query for correctness; the global !important kills them anyway. I'll rely on global (keeps module slim), but add explicit `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { animation:none }` in module for self-containment... redundant but harmless; skip — global covers.

Now the one-off sprite rebuild script. Mirror vendor script's sprite build: symbol id name, viewBox from source file, children of source svg into symbol. Node implementation with regex — safe since files are validated, uniform: `<svg xmlns="..." width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 -960 960 960"><path .../></svg>`.

Write temp script to opencode temp dir, run with node, replacing v5/public/assets/icons/material-symbols-rounded.svg, keeping existing 25 + adding 5 (order: existing + new). Easiest: rebuild FULL sprite from the SYNAMES list = existing 25 + new 5. Deterministic.

Then vendor-material-icons.py SYMBOLS list add the 5 names (so future python runs produce identical output).

Node script (ESM via .mjs):

```js
import fs from "fs";
import path from "path";
const root = "C:\\Users\\hi\\renewsejongpac-3\\v5\\public\\assets\\icons";
const NAMES = [ ...existing25..., "refresh", "home", "undo", "content_copy", "open_in_new" ];
const symbols = NAMES.map(name => {
  const source = fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, "rounded", name + ".svg"), "utf8");
  const viewBox = source.match(/viewBox="([^"]+)"/)[1];
  const inner = source.replace(/^[\s\S]*?<svg[^>]*>/, "").replace(/<\/svg>\s*$/, "");
  return `<symbol id="${name}" viewBox="${viewBox}">${inner}</symbol>`;
});
fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, "material-symbols-rounded.svg"),
  `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">` + symbols.join("") + `</svg>\n`);
```

Existing current sprite had final `</svg>\n` — match format: ET.tostring produces single-line. Good.

Sync-out will copy to v5 root? Sprite lives in v5/public/... — Next out includes assets (static). After rebuild, need re-run sync or rebuild? out/ was built earlier; public assets copy into out at build. Adding sprite symbols without rebuild → deployed v5/public? Actually the site loads sprite from /v5/assets/icons/... — which resolves to repo v5/public/assets? The deployed path: out contains public assets copied (Next copies public/ into out). v5 root after sync has v5/assets? sync copies outDir(v5/out) → v5 root: out/assets/... → v5/assets... Sprite file therefore also exists at v5/assets/icons/material-symbols-rounded.svg (synced copy). I must update BOTH or re sync. Simplest after all edits: run `npm run build` again (fast enough) OR run node scripts/sync-out.js to refresh v5/assets copy. Do sync-out at the end (no rebuild needed for pure asset/text changes? BUT context menu TSX + CSS changes require rebuild to appear in static output!). So final: full `npm run build` after implementing, then verify, then commit+push.

