parts.text:
Now the ContextMenu component. Design decisions:

- Client component with portal to body.
- Items: 새로 고침 (refresh), [링크] 새 창에서 열기 (open_in_new), 링크/페이지 주소 복사 (content_copy), 이전 페이지로 (undo), 홈으로 (home).
- Footer: when link target, show host/URL small text (useful info).
- Behavior: document contextmenu → if inside input/textarea/select/contenteditable → let native menu work; else preventDefault, open custom at pointer coords. In React SyntheticEvent terms, listen on document via window event.
- Position clamp: measure in useLayoutEffect.
- Keyboard: Escape close; ArrowUp/Down/Tab navigate items; focus first item on open.
- Close on outside pointerdown + window blur + scroll(capture, passive) + resize.
- History back: if window.history.length <= 1 → disable item (state-aware toast? just disabled).
- Copy: navigator.clipboard with execCommand fallback; showToast.
- Cute modern look per tokens: white surface (--paper), radius banner clamp (~22px, but prefer fixed 24px per large-modal contract → use clamp like --radius-banner? contract large modals 24px → `border-radius: 1.5rem`), border 1px --line, shadow 0 0.5rem 1.5rem rgba, padding 8px, items min-height 44px? Contract: 일반 조작 48px → min-height: 48px with gap, hover bg --soft (같은 색), pressed --color-gray-300-ish, focus-visible global outline applies (3px black + 4px offset inside menu could clash with rounded border — outline-offset 4px beyond border OK).
- Icon: Icon component (raw names work: names[name]||name).
- Animation: entrance scale(0.96)→1 + opacity, 160ms ease-out; transform-origin top-left-ish: use origin based on quadrant? simple: origin top left when plenty of space below-right (we clamp anyway). Reduced motion handled globally (durations → 0.01ms anyway) + explicit media query in module to be self-contained.
- aria: role="menu" aria-label "페이지 컨텍스트 메뉴"? Use aria-label="바로가기 메뉴"? Keep "컨텍스트 메뉴" role menu; items role="menuitem", each button type=button. Host footer aria-hidden? no, it's info: role="presentation"? Keep as small div (not interactive) — fine.

Extra: also disable native context menu & selection in HomeAnchorNavigation/header? Not needed.

Edge: right-click on links inside <body> — target closest('a'); href may be undefined for <a> without href (skip then). Also on already-open menu right-click → close & reopen at new point (preventDefault; target closest('a') none; maybe target inside menu — treat: if click within menu → preventDefault & keep open? Simpler: preventDefault, reopen at new coords... could feel odd but fine: adopt reopen.

Mobile long-press: fires contextmenu after ~500ms on links/images. preventDefault → prevents native link menu; our menu appears. Also prevent default selectstart? Already no selection. For touch, menu overlaps finger area → clamp.

Also include "이 페이지 소스 복사"? no. Add "인쇄"? Not necessary; keep 5 actions max (minimal).

history.back: act as undo. If no history (length<=1 or performance.navigation==0): disable → style disabled.

Write component now. TSX types carefully.

Clamp logic: menu w/h via offsetWidth/offsetHeight after mount with initial visibility hidden? React 18: first render at (x,y) → useEffect measures → setState clamped. To avoid visible jump, set style visibility 'hidden' until measured single frame: useLayoutEffect runs synchronously before paint → safe to measure & clamp in same layout effect without flicker (element rendered but not painted; mutations invisible). So: render at x,y; in useLayoutEffect: measure rect, compute clamped coords, set style via ref directly (no state) → zero flicker.

Keyboard focus: focus first item in same layout effect (focus steals w/o scroll: preventScroll true).

Arrows: keydown on menu container.

Code:

```tsx
"use client";

import React, { useEffect, useLayoutEffect, useRef, useState, useCallback } from "react";
import { createPortal } from "react-dom";
import Icon from "./Icon";
import { showToast } from "./Toast";
import styles from "./ContextMenu.module.css";

interface MenuState {
    x: number;
    y: number;
    href: string | null;
}

type SYMBOL = ... use raw names: "refresh","open_in_new","content_copy","undo","home".

export default function ContextMenu() {
    const [menu, setMenu] = useState<MenuState | null>(null);
    const [canGoBack, setCanGoBack] = useState(true);
    const shellRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement | null>(null);
    const listRef = useRef<HTMLUListElement>? use div; keep role=menu on div wrapping buttons.

    useEffect(() => {
        const open = (e: event) => {
            const target = e.target as HTMLElement | null;
            if (target?.closest('input, textarea, select, [contenteditable="true"]')) return;
            e.preventDefault();
            const anchor = target?.closest("a[href]") as HTMLAnchorElement | null;
            setCanGoBack(window.history.length > 1);
            setMenu({ x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY, href: anchor?.href ?? null });
        };
        document.addEventListener("contextmenu", open);
        return () => document.removeEventListener("contextmenu", open);
    }, []);
```

Wait: setCanGoBack via history.length — SPA Next static export: history length changes; fine.

When open changes to non-null: add outside-close listeners; on null: remove. Implement second effect keyed by menu!=null.

Position clamp in useLayoutEffect [menu]:

```tsx
useLayoutEffect(() => {
    if (!menu || !shellRef.current) return;
    const shell = shellRef.current;
    const rect = shell.getBoundingClientRect();
    const margin = 12;
    let x = menu.x, y = menu.y;
    if (x + rect.width + margin > window.innerWidth) x = window.innerWidth - rect.width - margin;
    if (y + rect.height + margin > window.innerHeight) y = window.innerHeight - rect.height - margin;
    x = Math.max(margin, x);
    y = Math.max(margin, y);
    shell.style.left = `${x}px`;
    shell.style.top = `${y}px`;
    const first = shell.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("button[data-menu-item]");
    if (first) first.focus({ preventScroll: true });
}, [menu, open?]);
